      "output": "**Focus this week:**\u202fFinalize your internship CV while keeping daily programming\u2011exam prep consistent.\n\n**Why:**\u202fThe CV is a single deliverable you can complete in a few focused sessions, and steady coding practice will keep the exam material fresh for the test in 10\u202fdays.\n\n**Day\u2011by\u2011day plan**\n\n| Day | CV work | Exam prep |\n|-----|---------|-----------|\n| 1 | Outline sections (contact, education, projects, experience) | 1\u202fhour: review core language syntax |\n| 2 | Draft bullet points for each project (focus on impact, tech used) | 1\u202fhour: solve 2 easy coding problems |\n| 3 | Write experience descriptions; tailor language to internship role | 1\u202fhour: revisit key algorithms (sorting, recursion) |\n| 4 | Refine formatting, ensure consistency, add keywords | 1\u202fhour: practice timed problem set (medium difficulty) |\n| 5 | Peer\u2011review or read aloud for clarity; incorporate feedback | 1\u202fhour: review past exam topics, note weak spots |\n| 6 | Final edit, proofread, export PDF | 1\u202fhour: mock exam under timed conditions |\n| 7 | Send CV to target company / upload to portal | 1\u202fhour: quick recap of any remaining weak areas |\n\n**Next step:**\u202fBlock two 1\u2011hour slots each day\u2014one for CV work, one for exam prep\u2014and let me know if you have any fixed commitments this week that would require adjusting the schedule.",
