      },
      "output": "**Recommendation:** Pursue an internal transition to a data\u2011science\u2011focused role at your current company while building a portfolio of applied ML projects on the side.\n\n**Trade\u2011off:** This path lets you leverage your existing network and salary base (low risk, high reversibility) but requires you to demonstrate concrete data\u2011science competence beyond your analyst duties, which means a short, intensive up\u2011skill and project sprint.\n\n**Next actions**\n\n1. **Skill sprint (Weeks\u202f1\u20114):** Complete a focused ML course (e.g., Coursera \u201cMachine Learning\u201d or a German\u2011language equivalent) and finish the associated capstone that produces a reproducible model on a public dataset.  \n2. **Internal pitch (Week\u202f5):** Draft a one\u2011page proposal showing how you can apply the new model to a current business problem (e.g., demand forecasting or churn prediction) and request a 20\u202f%\u2011time allocation from your manager to prototype it.  \n3. **Portfolio build (Weeks\u202f6\u20118):** Deliver the prototype, document the process, and add the notebook + results to a public GitHub repo; update your LinkedIn and internal profile to highlight the data\u2011science deliverable.  \n\n*Is there a specific business area at your company where you think a predictive model could add immediate value?*",
