      },
      "output": "**Long\u2011weekend city break \u2013 Lisbon, Portugal**  \nLisbon offers a compact historic centre, a thriving caf\u00e9 culture and late\u2011morning flight options from Manchester, matching your slow\u2011travel, one\u2011city vibe.\n\n**Day\u202f1 \u2013 Arrival & settle**  \nFly out of Manchester mid\u2011morning (e.g., 10\u202fam) to Lisbon; take the Aerobus to the Baixa district, check into a boutique hotel or well\u2011located Airbnb (preferably with a small kitchen). Spend the afternoon wandering the Rua Augusta promenade, then unwind at *Caf\u00e9 A Brasileira* in Chiado for a coffee and pastel de nata.\n\n**Day\u202f2 \u2013 Alfama & river views**  \nLate start (breakfast at *Pois Caf\u00e9*). Explore the winding Alfama streets, visit S\u00e3o\u202fJorge Castle for panoramic city views, and stop at *F\u00e1brica Lisboa* for specialty coffee. Evening: dine at a riverside restaurant in Cais do Sodr\u00e9 and enjoy a fado show (book the venue now).\n\n**Day\u202f3 \u2013 Bel\u00e9m & caf\u00e9 hopping**  \nTake tram\u202f15 to Bel\u00e9m after a relaxed morning. Must\u2011do: Past\u00e9is de Bel\u00e9m bakery, Jer\u00f3nimos Monastery (tickets online), and the MAAT museum. In the afternoon, hop between *Nicolau Lisboa* and *Hello, Kristof* for different caf\u00e9 atmospheres. Return to the city centre for a sunset at the Miradouro da Senhora do Monte.\n\n**Day\u202f4 \u2013 Market stroll & departure**  \nSleep in, then brunch at *The Mill* (London\u2011style coffee). Browse the Mercado da Ribeira (Time Out Market) for local bites and souvenirs. Catch a late\u2011afternoon flight (e.g., 4\u202fpm) back to Manchester, giving you a relaxed final day.\n\n**Book\u2011now items**  \n- Manchester\u202f\u2192\u202fLisbon flight (avoid early\u2011morning departures)  \n- Central accommodation (preferably with kitchen)  \n- Fado venue tickets for Day\u202f2 evening  \n- Jer\u00f3nimos Monastery entry (optional guided tour)\n\n**Decide\u2011later items**  \n- Specific restaurant reservations for dinner (flexible)  \n- Optional day\u2011trip to Sintra (could be added if you find extra time)  \n\n**External checks**  \n- Verify visa\u2011free entry for UK citizens (generally not required for short stays).  \n- Check the weather forecast for late\u2011spring/early\u2011summer (pleasant but occasional rain).  \n\n*What dates are you targeting for this long weekend?*",
