      "output": "**Assumption:** You need a cash deposit for a flat in Dublin in\u202f3\u202fyears and want a clear monthly savings target.\n\n**Target calculation**  \n1. **Estimate the deposit size.** In Dublin, a typical 10\u202f% deposit on a modest two\u2011bedroom flat is often around \u20ac30\u202f000\u2013\u20ac40\u202f000. Choose a middle point, e.g. \u20ac35\u202f000.  \n2. **Add a safety buffer.** Set aside an extra 5\u202f% (\u2248\u202f\u20ac1\u202f750) for closing costs, moving expenses, or a short\u2011term market dip. Target total\u202f\u2248\u202f\u20ac36\u202f750.  \n3. **Convert to a monthly goal.** \u20ac36\u202f750 \u00f7 36\u202fmonths\u202f\u2248\u202f\u20ac1\u202f020 per month.\n\n**Why this works** \u2013 Saving roughly \u20ac1\u202f000 each month meets the deposit plus buffer without relying on large windfalls. It respects the cash\u2011flow constraint (you must still cover rent, utilities, food, transport, and any debt payments). The 5\u202f% buffer protects you if a month\u2019s net income falls short.\n\n**Downside test** \u2013 Suppose you lose \u20ac500 of net income for a month (e.g., reduced hours). If you keep the \u20ac1\u202f020 target, you\u2019d need to dip into existing savings or cut discretionary spending. To avoid that, keep a 1\u2011month emergency fund of at least \u20ac2\u202f000 (about two weeks of expenses) that you can draw on before breaking the savings cadence.\n\n**Next actions (you can start this week)**  \n1. **Set up an automatic transfer** of \u20ac1\u202f020 from your checking to a high\u2011interest savings account on payday.  \n2. **Build a \u20ac2\u202f000 emergency buffer** (if you don\u2019t have one) by allocating any surplus or a one\u2011off bonus before the regular savings start.  \n3. **Track monthly cash flow** in a simple spreadsheet or budgeting app to confirm you can sustain the \u20ac1\u202f020 contribution without overspending.\n\n*Is \u20ac35\u202f000 a realistic estimate for the flat you have in mind, or would you prefer a higher or lower deposit target?*",
