      "output": "**Assumption:**\u202fYou\u2019re doing a 4\u2011day upper/lower split, have dumbbells (up to ~20\u202fkg) and a pull\u2011up bar at home, and will be equipment\u2011free Thursday\u202f&\u202fFriday while traveling.\n\n### This Week (7\u202fdays)\n\n| Day | Session | Main Moves (sets\u202f\u00d7\u202freps) | Notes |\n|-----|---------|--------------------------|-------|\n| Mon | Upper\u202fA | DB Bench Press\u202f3\u00d78\u201110<br>Pull\u2011ups (or band\u2011assisted)\u202f3\u00d76\u20118<br>One\u2011Arm DB Row\u202f3\u00d78\u201110 each side<br>DB Lateral Raise\u202f2\u00d712\u201115<br>Triceps DB Overhead Press\u202f2\u00d710\u201112 | Use a weight that leaves 2\u20113 reps \u201cin the tank\u201d on the last set. |\n| Tue | Lower\u202fA | Goblet Squat\u202f3\u00d710\u201112<br>Romanian DB Deadlift\u202f3\u00d78\u201110<br>Walking DB Lunge\u202f2\u00d712 each leg<br>Glute Bridge (bodyweight)\u202f2\u00d715\u201120<br>Plank\u202f3\u00d730\u202fs | Keep tempo steady (2\u20110\u20112). |\n| Wed | Upper\u202fB | Incline DB Press\u202f3\u00d78\u201110<br>Chin\u2011ups (or band\u2011assisted)\u202f3\u00d76\u20118<br>DB Bent\u2011over Reverse Fly\u202f2\u00d712\u201115<br>DB Hammer Curl\u202f2\u00d710\u201112<br>Face Pulls with band\u202f2\u00d715\u201120 | Same load rule as Monday. |\n| Thu | Travel (no gear) | **Bodyweight Circuit** \u2013 3 rounds: 15\u202fpush\u2011ups, 20\u202fair\u2011squats, 30\u2011s plank, 10\u202fburpees | Keep total time \u2264\u202f20\u202fmin; focus on movement quality. |\n| Fri | Travel (no gear) | **Mobility & Core** \u2013 2\u202f\u00d7\u202f: 30\u202fs each side side\u2011plank, 20\u202fbird\u2011dogs, 30\u202fs hip\u2011flexor stretch, 15\u202fsupermans | Light, recovery\u2011oriented. |\n| Sat | Lower\u202fB | Bulgarian Split Squat (DB held)\u202f3\u00d78\u201110 each leg<br>Single\u2011Leg Romanian DB Deadlift\u202f3\u00d78\u201110 each leg<br>Calf Raise (bodyweight or holding DB)\u202f3\u00d715\u201120<br>Leg\u2011Raise (hanging if bar available, else floor)\u202f3\u00d710\u201112 | If pull\u2011up bar is accessible, hang for leg\u2011raises; otherwise floor version. |\n| Sun | Rest or active recovery (walk, light stretching) | \u2013 | \u2013 |\n\n**Progression rule:**\u202fEach week try to add 1\u20132\u202fkg to dumbbell lifts or 1 extra rep per set, while keeping form. If you can\u2019t add weight, add a rep or slow the tempo (e.g., 3\u2011sec eccentric). Deload every 4\u20115\u202fweeks by dropping the load ~20\u202f% or cutting one set.\n\n**Busy\u2011week fallback:**\u202fIf any day feels too tight, replace the full session with the 15\u2011minute bodyweight circuit (push\u2011ups, squats, plank, burpees) and keep the other days as planned.  \n\nDo you have any current injuries or movement limitations I should consider?",
