      "output": "Focus this week on two high\u2011impact blocks:\n\n1. **Programming exam preparation** \u2013 allocate the bulk of your time to reviewing core topics and doing timed practice problems.  \n2. **Internship CV** \u2013 finish a polished draft and get feedback before you shift fully to the exam.\n\n**Suggested schedule (Day\u202f1\u20117)**  \n\n| Day | Main focus | Action |\n|-----|------------|--------|\n| 1   | Exam prep  | Review the syllabus outline; identify three weakest topics. |\n| 2   | Exam prep  | Solve 2\u20133 practice problems per weak topic (no more than 90\u202fmin). |\n| 3   | CV draft   | Write the \u201cExperience\u201d section, using concise bullet points. |\n| 4   | Exam prep  | Do a 60\u2011minute timed mock test; note errors. |\n| 5   | CV draft   | Complete \u201cEducation\u201d and \u201cSkills\u201d sections; insert placeholders for any missing projects. |\n| 6   | Exam prep  | Review mock\u2011test errors; redo those problem types. |\n| 7   | CV review  | Send the draft to a trusted peer or mentor for feedback; incorporate quick edits. |\n\n**Next step:**\u202fStart Day\u202f1 by listing the three topics you feel least confident about for the programming exam. Let me know which they are, and I can suggest focused resources.",
