        "words": 392,
        "violations": []
      },
      "output": "**Assumption:** You have a full\u2011day schedule aside from classes and need focused, active\u2011recall sessions to cover all thermodynamics topics before the exam on the 20th.\n\n**Two\u2011week study plan (Day\u202f1\u202f\u2013\u202fDay\u202f14)**  \n\n| Day | Activity |\n|-----|----------|\n| 1 | Review lecture notes on the First Law; write a one\u2011page summary in your own words and create 5 flashcards for the key equations. |\n| 2 | Solve 4 practice problems on internal energy changes for ideal gases; check each step against the solution manual. |\n| 3 | Watch a 20\u2011minute video on entropy concepts; then explain the concept aloud as if teaching a peer and note any gaps. |\n| 4 | Do a mixed\u2011problem set (3\u202f\u00d7\u202fFirst Law, 2\u202f\u00d7\u202fEntropy); after finishing, rewrite any incorrect solutions without looking at the answer key. |\n| 5 | Create a mind map linking heat transfer modes (conduction, convection, radiation) to governing equations; review it twice spaced apart. |\n| 6 | Practice 5 problems on reversible vs. irreversible processes; for each, state why the process is classified as such. |\n| 7 | Take a 30\u2011minute timed quiz covering Chapters\u202f1\u20113 (no notes); immediately grade and identify weak items. |\n| 8 | Review weak items from Day\u202f7; redo those problems with a different approach (e.g., using a diagram). |\n| 9 | Study the Second Law derivations; derive the Carnot efficiency formula on a blank sheet, then compare to the textbook version. |\n| 10 | Solve 4 cycle\u2011analysis problems (Otto, Diesel, Brayton); after each, sketch the corresponding P\u2011V diagram from memory. |\n| 11 | Teach a 10\u2011minute mini\u2011lecture to a study buddy or record yourself explaining exergy; note any stumbling points. |\n| 12 | Complete a full\u2011length past exam (no timing pressure); mark all questions you\u2019re unsure about. |\n| 13 | Review marked questions from Day\u202f12; consult the textbook for theory, then re\u2011solve each problem without looking at solutions. |\n| 14 | Light review: flip through flashcards, revisit the mind map, and do a 15\u2011minute rapid\u2011recall test covering all major formulas. |\n\n**Next step you can start today:** Write the one\u2011page summary of the First Law (Day\u202f1 activity) and create the five flashcards.  \n\n*Did the outline feel realistic for the amount of time you can dedicate each day?*",
      "judge": {
        "passed": true,
        "available": true,
        "dimensions": {
