      "output": "**Long\u2011weekend caf\u00e9\u2011focused city break (Friday\u2011Sunday)**  \n\n**Why it fits:** A single, walkable city with a thriving caf\u00e9 scene, reachable from Manchester on a mid\u2011morning flight or train, lets you avoid early departures and keep a relaxed pace.\n\n**Day\u202f1 \u2013 Friday** \u2013 Arrive mid\u2011morning, check into a boutique hotel or a well\u2011rated B&B in the historic centre. Spend the afternoon strolling the main pedestrian streets, stopping at a flagship specialty coffee shop for a welcome brew. Evening: dine at a restaurant with a relaxed vibe and optional night\u2011cap at a nearby bar.\n\n**Day\u202f2 \u2013 Saturday** \u2013 Morning: leisurely brunch at a popular brunch\u2011caf\u00e9 (reserve if possible). Mid\u2011day: explore a museum or gallery that matches your interests (e.g., art, history, design). Late afternoon: unwind in a park or riverside walk, with a stop at a second\u2011favorite caf\u00e9 for an afternoon tea or cold brew. Evening: attend a low\u2011key live\u2011music session or theatre show, then a late dinner at a locally\u2011sourced eatery.\n\n**Day\u202f3 \u2013 Sunday** \u2013 Late breakfast at a third\u2011recommended caf\u00e9 (perhaps one known for pastries). Use the rest of the day for a self\u2011guided walking tour of a neighbourhood famed for its street art, independent shops, or historic market. Finish with a relaxed dinner at a cosy spot before heading back to the accommodation.\n\n**Day\u202f4 \u2013 Monday (optional)** \u2013 If you have a half\u2011day free before travel, enjoy a final coffee on a terrace, then catch a late\u2011morning train or flight back to Manchester.\n\n**Book now**  \n- Transport: mid\u2011morning flight or train tickets (Manchester \u2194\u202fcity) \u2013 seats can fill quickly for weekend travel.  \n- Accommodation: boutique hotel/B&B in the historic centre (rooms limited).  \n\n**Decide later**  \n- Caf\u00e9 reservations (if the venue takes bookings).  \n- Museum/gallery tickets (especially for special exhibitions).  \n- Evening entertainment (concert, theatre) \u2013 check schedules closer to the date.\n\n**Next step:** Which city appeals most to you\u2014Dublin, Edinburgh, or another nearby destination with a strong caf\u00e9 culture?",
