      "output": "**Pick \u2013 iPhone SE (3rd\u202fgen, 2022)**  \n- **Why it fits:** It runs the full iOS ecosystem you already use, stays under \u00a3700 (typically \u00a3429\u202f\u2013\u202f\u00a3479), and offers a modern A15 Bionic chip that will handle everyday apps, photos and occasional gaming for years. Its small 4.7\u2011inch screen matches the size you\u2019re used to if you prefer a compact phone, and the single\u2011camera system still shoots excellent 12\u202fMP photos and 4K video. Battery life is decent for a day\u2011to\u2011day device, and Apple\u2019s long\u2011term software support means you can keep it for the 4+\u202fyears you like.\n\n**Runner\u2011up \u2013 iPhone 13\u202fmini**  \n- **Why it\u2019s close:** Same A15 processor, better dual\u2011camera system (wide\u202f+\u202fultrawide) and a brighter 5.4\u2011inch OLED display, which is a step up for media consumption. Prices on the used or refurbished market often sit in the \u00a3550\u202f\u2013\u202f\u00a3650 range, still within your budget, though new units may breach it. It\u2019s slightly larger and pricier, but gives you more screen real\u2011estate and better low\u2011light photography.\n\n**Decisive trade\u2011off:** The SE saves money and stays compact, while the 13\u202fmini gives a superior display and extra camera flexibility at a modest extra cost. If you value a larger, sharper screen for video and photos, lean toward the 13\u202fmini; if you want the cheapest, longest\u2011supported iPhone that meets all core needs, the SE is the better value.\n\n**Next steps**  \n1. Verify current pricing (new, certified\u2011refurbished, or reputable second\u2011hand) to ensure you stay under your \u00a3700 ceiling.  \n2. Check storage options \u2013 128\u202fGB is a safe baseline for a phone you\u2019ll keep several years.  \n3. Compare warranty/AppleCare+ costs if you want extra protection.\n\n**One quick question:** Do you prefer a compact 4.7\u2011inch phone or are you happy with the slightly larger 5.4\u2011inch display of the 13\u202fmini?",
