      },
      "output": "**Assumption:** You want to save the full deposit for a flat in Dublin over the next\u202f3\u202fyears and have a regular cash\u2011flow you can allocate each month.\n\n### Target amount\nA typical first\u2011time\u2011buyer deposit in Dublin is 10\u201120\u202f% of the purchase price. Assuming a modest target price of \u20ac350\u202fk, a 15\u202f% deposit would be \u20ac52,500. Adjust the percentage to match the price you expect; the calculation is:\n\n`Deposit\u202f=\u202fPurchase\u2011price\u202f\u00d7\u202fdesired\u2011deposit\u2011%`\n\n### Monthly savings needed\nDivide the total by 36\u202fmonths:\n\n`Monthly\u202ftarget\u202f\u2248\u202f\u20ac52,500\u202f\u00f7\u202f36\u202f\u2248\u202f\u20ac1,460`\n\nRound up to a comfortable round number (e.g., \u20ac1,500) to give a small buffer for fees or price changes.\n\n### Down\u2011side test\nIf a bad month cuts your net cash flow by \u20ac500 (e.g., unexpected bill), you could:\n\n1. Use a 1\u2011month emergency buffer (see next step) to cover the shortfall, **or**\n2. Reduce the monthly contribution that month and make up the difference later, extending the timeline slightly.\n\nEither way, the plan remains viable as long as you keep a cash\u2011flow cushion.\n\n### Quick framework & next actions\n1. **Build a 1\u2011month emergency fund** \u2013 aim for \u20ac1,500 in a high\u2011interest savings account before committing the full \u20ac1,500/month to the deposit fund.  \n2. **Open a dedicated \u201cflat\u2011deposit\u201d account** \u2013 keep it separate from everyday spending; automate a standing order for the monthly target.  \n3. **Track progress monthly** \u2013 compare actual contribution to the \u20ac1,500 goal; if you fall short, note the shortfall and plan a catch\u2011up month later.\n\nThese steps give you a clear target, protect you from occasional cash\u2011flow shocks, and keep the plan on track.\n\n*What is your current monthly net cash flow (after fixed expenses) so I can suggest a realistic portion to allocate to the deposit?*",
