      "output": "**Assumption:** You have a solid foundation in basic thermodynamics concepts and need focused review and practice to solidify problem\u2011solving skills before the final on the 20th.\n\n**Two\u2011week study plan (Day\u202f1\u202f\u2013\u202fDay\u202f14)**  \n\n| Day | Focus |\n|-----|-------|\n| 1 | Review core laws (0\u2011th, 1st, 2nd) and their mathematical statements; write one example for each. |\n| 2 | Study properties of pure substances (P\u2011v\u2011T tables, Mollier diagram); solve two tabular problems. |\n| 3 | Work through reversible and irreversible processes; compare entropy change calculations. |\n| 4 | Practice ideal\u2011gas cycles (Otto, Diesel, Brayton); derive efficiency formulas. |\n| 5 | Review psychrometrics basics; complete a humidity\u2011ratio problem set. |\n| 6 | Solve mixed\u2011phase problems (boiling, condensation) using energy balances. |\n| 7 | Mid\u2011point self\u2011test: 10 mixed\u2011topic problems under timed conditions; identify weak spots. |\n| 8 | Re\u2011visit weak topics from Day\u202f7; redo those problems with step\u2011by\u2011step notes. |\n| 9 | Study exergy analysis; calculate exergy destruction for a simple turbine. |\n|10 | Practice steady\u2011flow control volume problems (open system energy balance). |\n|11 | Review heat\u2011transfer correlations (conduction, convection, radiation) and apply to thermodynamic cycles. |\n|12 | Full\u2011length practice exam (20 problems, timed); simulate exam environment. |\n|13 | Review exam results; focus on any remaining errors; create a concise \u201ccheat sheet\u201d of key formulas. |\n|14 | Light review of cheat sheet; mental rehearsal of problem\u2011solving steps; ensure adequate rest.  \n\n**Next step:** Pick a problem from Day\u202f3 (entropy change for an irreversible expansion) and write out the full solution today. How comfortable do you feel with setting up the entropy balance for that case?",
