      "output": "**Lisbon, Portugal \u2013 a relaxed long\u2011weekend with caf\u00e9 culture and easy late\u2011day arrivals**\n\n*Lisbon fits a slow\u2011travel vibe, offers countless caf\u00e9s, and its main airport handles late\u2011afternoon flights from Manchester, avoiding early\u2011morning departures.*\n\n**Day\u202f1 \u2013 Arrival & first stroll**  \nFly Manchester \u2192 Lisbon (late afternoon, e.g., 16:30\u202f\u2013\u202f19:30 arrival). Take the Aerobus to Pra\u00e7a\u202fMarqu\u00eas de Pombal, check into a boutique hotel or well\u2011rated boutique guesthouse in the Baixa district. Evening walk down Rua\u202fGarcia\u202fPinto to the historic Alfama neighbourhood; dinner at a traditional tasca.\n\n**Day\u202f2 \u2013 Caf\u00e9 hopping & city sights**  \nLate breakfast at *Caf\u00e9 A Brasileira* in Chiado. Mid\u2011morning visit the S\u00e3o\u202fJorge Castle (use the tram 28 for a scenic ride). Lunch at *Time Out Market* (choose a stall that suits any dietary need). Afternoon coffee at *F\u00e1brica Coffee Roasters* near the river. Sunset at Miradouro da Senhora do Monte, then a relaxed dinner in Bairro Alto.\n\n**Day\u202f3 \u2013 Museum & river**  \nStart at *Manteigaria* for a pastel de nata and espresso. Visit the Calouste Gulbenkian Museum (quiet, art\u2011filled morning). Lunch at a riverside caf\u00e9 in Bel\u00e9m; try the famous *Past\u00e9is de Bel\u00e9m* (optional). Afternoon stroll along the Tagus, optional short boat ride (decide later). Evening free for a live Fado show in Alfama.\n\n**Day\u202f4 \u2013 Leisure & departure**  \nLate brunch at *Nicolau Lisboa* (healthy options). Spend the morning browsing independent book\u2011shops and vintage stores in the Pr\u00edncipe Real area. Return to the hotel, collect luggage, and catch a late\u2011afternoon flight (e.g., 15:30\u202f\u2013\u202f18:30) back to Manchester.\n\n**Key cost drivers**  \n- Flights (late\u2011day return tends to be cheaper)  \n- Central boutique accommodation (\u2248\u202f\u00a380\u2011\u00a3120 per night)  \n- Meals & caf\u00e9s (\u2248\u202f\u00a330\u2011\u00a350 per day)  \n- Museum entry & optional river boat (\u2248\u202f\u00a310\u2011\u00a320 total)\n\n**Book now**  \n- Manchester \u2192 Lisbon flight (late afternoon both ways)  \n- Central boutique hotel/guesthouse (ensure free cancellation)  \n\n**Decide later**  \n- River boat ticket (if desired)  \n- Fado venue reservation (most accept walk\u2011ins, but a table can be secured)  \n\n*Check visa\u2011free entry for UK citizens (currently allowed for short stays) and confirm opening hours for the castle and museum, as they can vary seasonally.*  \n\nWhat dates are you considering for this long weekend?",
