      "output": "**Pick:** iPhone\u202fSE (3rd\u202fgen, 2022) \u2013 \u00a3399\u202f\u2013\u202f\u00a3499 (new) or similar price refurbished.  \n*Why:* It stays in the Apple ecosystem, offers the A15 Bionic chip (same as iPhone\u202f13), 5\u202fG, solid camera, and a durable design that will comfortably last four\u202fyears. At under \u00a3700 it fits your budget and you can keep it long\u2011term without paying a premium for unnecessary size or features.\n\n**Runner\u2011up:** Refurbished iPhone\u202f13\u202fmini (or a lightly used iPhone\u202f13) \u2013 typically \u00a3500\u202f\u2013\u202f\u00a3650.  \n*Why:* Same performance and camera quality as the SE but in a smaller, higher\u2011quality OLED screen and with a longer\u2011lasting battery. It\u2019s a bit pricier, so you\u2019d be paying for a premium display you may not need.\n\n**Decisive trade\u2011off:** The SE gives you essentially flagship performance at a lower price and a proven, compact form factor, while the 13\u202fmini adds a better screen and battery at a modest cost increase. If screen quality is a priority, go the 13\u202fmini; otherwise the SE is the more cost\u2011efficient, future\u2011proof choice.\n\n**Next steps**  \n1. Check current pricing on Apple\u2019s refurbished store or reputable sellers (e.g., certified refurbishers).  \n2. Verify the device is unlocked or compatible with your carrier.  \n3. Consider AppleCare+ if you want extra protection for the four\u2011year lifespan.\n\n**Question:** Do you prefer a smaller \u201cpocket\u2011size\u201d phone (like the 13\u202fmini) or are you happy with the SE\u2019s slightly larger 4.7\u2011inch display?",
